# Example local settings for Microsoft Entra ID authentication only. Every other
# variable is documented in src/config.js. Copy to .env for `npm run dev` and keep
# .env out of Git. Use placeholders only: never put real secrets in this file.

# Microsoft Entra ID access-token validation (see README "Authentication").
# Leave both IDs empty locally: protected routes then return 401 and /health still works.
# Both are required when NODE_ENV is production, so they must be set in every CDP environment (cdp-app-config).
# Directory (tenant) ID of the Entra tenant that issues the tokens, a GUID.
ENTRA_TENANT_ID=
# Application (client) ID of the App Registration shared with the frontend, a GUID.
ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=
# Delegated scope the access token must grant, as it appears in the scp claim.
ENTRA_API_SCOPE=access_as_user
